## Step 4 — Choose One or More Design Concepts That Satisfy the Selected Drivers

**Decision**: Adopt **Hybrid Modular Monolith with Event-Driven Core and CQRS** architecture style.

**Drivers Addressed**: CON-1, CON-2, CON-4, CON-5, CON-6, CRN-1, CRN-2, CRN-3, CRN-4, CRN-5, QA-1, QA-2, QA-4, QA-6

**Rationale**: CQRS addresses QA-1 (query performance via read model) and QA-4 (scalability via independent read/write scaling). Async events via Kafka address QA-2 (reliability through event persistence) and QA-6 (modifiability through decoupled modules). Hybrid API Gateway pattern (sync queries, async commands with feedback) satisfies CON-5 and provides user feedback. MVP scope with logical CQRS (single DB, separate schemas) addresses CON-4.

**Alternatives Considered**: Monolithic Layered (rejected — not cloud-native, poor scalability); Full Microservices (rejected — too complex for MVP); Hybrid without CQRS (rejected — cannot achieve QA-1/QA-4 thresholds)

**Implications**: Eventual consistency between write and read models; API Gateway needs both synchronous and asynchronous handling; MVP uses logical CQRS (same DB, different schemas) to reduce complexity; full physical separation deferred.

