### Communication Pattern Details

**Command Flow (HPS-2: Change Prices) with Async Feedback:**
```
User → Angular SPA → API Gateway (REST POST /api/prices/change)
     → API Gateway generates tracking ID (UUID)
     → API Gateway publishes to Kafka "price-change-commands" topic with tracking ID
     → API Gateway returns HTTP 202 Accepted + tracking ID
     → Angular SPA displays "Price change submitted" with tracking ID
     → Angular SPA polls GET /api/prices/change/{trackingId}/status OR uses Server-Sent Events

     → Price Calculation Module consumes command from Kafka
     → Price Calculation Module executes Rate Calculation Engine (HPS-5 business rules)
     → Price Calculation Module updates PostgreSQL write_model schema (same transaction)
     → Price Calculation Module publishes to Kafka "price-change-events" topic with tracking ID
     → Query Module consumes event, updates read_model materialized view
     → Query Module updates status endpoint: "Price change complete"
     
     → Angular SPA polling detects completion → displays confirmation to user
```

**Query Flow (HPS-3: Query Prices):**
```
User/External System → API Gateway (REST GET /api/prices?hotel=X&dates=Y)
     → API Gateway validates JWT, checks hotel authorization
     → API Gateway calls Query Module via internal REST
     → Query Module reads from PostgreSQL read_model schema (materialized view)
     → Returns price data
API Gateway returns HTTP 200 with data
```

